WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.634 --> 00:00:02.734
-Welcome to "The Tonight Show
At Home Edition," everybody.

00:00:02.734 --> 00:00:04.534
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:00:04.534 --> 00:00:05.767
It is Wednesday!

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:06.901
Oh, yeah, man.
[ Snapping fingers ]

00:00:06.901 --> 00:00:08.100
That's what I'm talkin' about.

00:00:08.100 --> 00:00:10.901
Actually, it's almost
Thursday, basically.

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:13.033
So it's Thursday, kind of.

00:00:13.033 --> 00:00:14.701
You gettin' that vibe?
You gettin' that vibe from me?

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:15.968
Cool, cool, cool.

00:00:15.968 --> 00:00:18.734
Alright, let's get
to some news here, everybody!

00:00:18.734 --> 00:00:20.334
Tomorrow, President Trump
will be visiting

00:00:20.334 --> 00:00:23.400
a Ford plant in Michigan
that requires face masks,

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:26.267
but Trump said he's not sure
if he'll wear one.

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:27.667
Trump actually loves Ford,

00:00:27.667 --> 00:00:29.167
especially 'cause the "F"
in the logo

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:32.434
sort of looks like his hair.

00:00:32.434 --> 00:00:34.234
I think Trump might be
a little disappointed

00:00:34.234 --> 00:00:35.400
when he gets
to the Ford factory

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.200
'cause, once he walks in,
he's gonna be like,

00:00:37.200 --> 00:00:38.467
"When I asked to see
the new models,

00:00:38.467 --> 00:00:40.000
this is not what I meant."

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:43.734
Well, guys,
the election is coming up

00:00:43.734 --> 00:00:46.901
and everyone's debating
mail-in voting.

00:00:46.901 --> 00:00:48.234
Republicans are worried
old people

00:00:48.234 --> 00:00:50.167
will be confused
by a new system,

00:00:50.167 --> 00:00:51.467
while Democrats are worried
young people

00:00:51.467 --> 00:00:54.334
won't know how
to mail a letter.

00:00:54.334 --> 00:00:57.400
Check this out -- I saw
that the NFL is testing helmets

00:00:57.400 --> 00:01:00.934
that have an N95 face mask
built into them.

00:01:00.934 --> 00:01:02.701
Yeah. And, if that works,

00:01:02.701 --> 00:01:04.434
football will be
completely safe.

00:01:06.834 --> 00:01:09.234
People are talking about this --
last night, in Chicago,

00:01:09.234 --> 00:01:10.734
the Willis Tower lost power

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:12.534
and it looked
like it had a face.

00:01:12.534 --> 00:01:13.968
Take a look.

00:01:13.968 --> 00:01:15.400
That tower looks like it's got
a serious case

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:17.767
of resting building face.

00:01:17.767 --> 00:01:19.667
That looks like every LEGO,
hiding in the dark,

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:22.133
[ Laughing ]
waiting for me to step on it.

00:01:22.133 --> 00:01:24.367
Some TV news --
Kristen Cavallari announced

00:01:24.367 --> 00:01:27.968
that she is ending her reality
show "Very Cavallari."

00:01:27.968 --> 00:01:30.634
It's very sad. Earlier today
on the E! network,

00:01:30.634 --> 00:01:33.467
the exclamation point was
changed to a somber period.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:38.234
This went viral this week --
apparently, Chuck E. Cheese

00:01:38.234 --> 00:01:42.100
realized that nobody was
ordering their pizza as takeout,

00:01:42.100 --> 00:01:44.367
so they changed their name
on delivery apps

00:01:44.367 --> 00:01:47.200
to Pasqually's Pizza,

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.434
after a member
of their robotic band.

00:01:50.434 --> 00:01:53.267
I guess there's a member
called Pasqually,

00:01:53.267 --> 00:01:54.901
so, Pasqually's Pizza.

00:01:54.901 --> 00:01:56.133
They basically tried
to trick people

00:01:56.133 --> 00:01:57.767
into ordering Chuck E. Cheese.

00:01:57.767 --> 00:02:00.767
Well, today we found out
they're not the only ones.

00:02:00.767 --> 00:02:02.801
Check out this commercial
I just saw.

00:02:02.801 --> 00:02:05.901
-[ French accent ]
Stop searching for the next
culinary revelation

00:02:05.901 --> 00:02:08.400
[ French tune plays ]
and experience ze excellence,

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:10.601
taste the magnificence,

00:02:10.601 --> 00:02:12.834
indulge in the elegance

00:02:12.834 --> 00:02:14.801
at Grimace's Bistro,

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:16.267
available on delivery apps

00:02:16.267 --> 00:02:19.834
or le drive-through.

00:02:19.834 --> 00:02:21.534
-Looks pretty good, actually.

00:02:21.534 --> 00:02:24.033
I just saw that, for the summer,
Absolut unveiled

00:02:24.033 --> 00:02:26.834
the new line
of ready-to-drink vodka sodas.

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:29.300
'Cause that was always
the problem with vodka sodas --

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:31.367
they took way
too much time to make.

00:02:33.267 --> 00:02:39.501
You gotta put the vodka
and the soda...

00:02:39.501 --> 00:02:42.100
Sometimes you do the soda,
instead of the vodka.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:44.000
You do the vodka and the soda.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.634
Soda, the vodka, soda.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:49.100
You do the soda.

00:02:49.100 --> 00:02:51.267
This is crazy --
a grocery store in Missouri

00:02:51.267 --> 00:02:53.868
had apparently replaced
all the items in their salad bar

00:02:53.868 --> 00:02:55.868
[ Laughing ]
with tiny liquor bottles.

00:02:55.868 --> 00:02:58.267
Take a look at this.

00:02:58.267 --> 00:03:00.400
The hard part was picking up
the liquor bottles

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.767
with the salad tongs.

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:04.834
They also renamed
the sneeze guard

00:03:04.834 --> 00:03:06.801
to the puke roof.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:09.067
[ Chuckle ]
Check this out --

00:03:09.067 --> 00:03:11.200
I saw that the Belmont Stakes
is now scheduled

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.067
to take place
before the Kentucky Derby.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:17.067
Racing fans were outraged,
while the horses continue

00:03:17.067 --> 00:03:19.200
to have no idea what's going on.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.701
Guys, that's our monologue,
right there.

00:03:20.701 --> 00:03:22.634
We have a awesome show tonight!

00:03:22.634 --> 00:03:24.767
Anthony Anderson is here
[ Clap ] tonight!

00:03:24.767 --> 00:03:27.501
Michelle Dockery is here;
and, of course,

00:03:27.501 --> 00:03:30.400
we have great, great music
from Gary Clark Jr.

00:03:30.400 --> 00:03:32.167
Hey, everyone. It's Wednesday,
which means it's time

00:03:32.167 --> 00:03:33.868
for "What Are You Doing
Wednesday."

00:03:33.868 --> 00:03:35.167
-♪ What are you doin'? ♪

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:36.534
♪ It's Wednesday ♪

00:03:36.534 --> 00:03:37.834
♪ What are you doin'? ♪

00:03:37.834 --> 00:03:39.300
♪ It's Wednesday ♪

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:40.501
♪♪

00:03:40.501 --> 00:03:42.701
-These are videos
that I've seen online

00:03:42.701 --> 00:03:44.767
that you guys are all making
'cause we're all inside

00:03:44.767 --> 00:03:46.567
and doing something,
trying to be creative.

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:49.667
I think these are my favorite
videos I've seen this week,

00:03:49.667 --> 00:03:51.234
so, thank you.
Keep making these videos

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:52.234
and I'll find them.

00:03:52.234 --> 00:03:54.200
This first one is from Maryland.

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:55.634
It's a restaurant
that thought of a fun way

00:03:55.634 --> 00:03:57.801
for diners to socially distance.

00:03:57.801 --> 00:03:58.901
Check it out.

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:07.234
♪♪

00:04:07.234 --> 00:04:09.934
♪♪

00:04:09.934 --> 00:04:12.167
-[ Laughs ]
It's all fun and games

00:04:12.167 --> 00:04:15.934
until Barb gets bumped
into the lake.

00:04:15.934 --> 00:04:19.434
This next one is from @kpakster.

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:20.601
They were bored
during quarantine,

00:04:20.601 --> 00:04:22.934
so he and a friend
made up a game

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.834
with a broken Walgreens sign.

00:04:24.834 --> 00:04:26.133
[ Laughing ]
Check this out.

00:04:26.133 --> 00:04:27.133
-Walg.
-Greens.

00:04:27.133 --> 00:04:28.133
Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:28.868
-Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:30.767
-Greens. Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:30.767 --> 00:04:31.567
-Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:31.567 --> 00:04:33.300
-Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:33.934
-Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:35.367
-Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:35.367 --> 00:04:36.367
-Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:36.367 --> 00:04:38.300
-Greens.
-Walg.

00:04:38.300 --> 00:04:41.434
They did that for eight hours.

00:04:41.434 --> 00:04:42.834
This next one's
from Kate Sibbick.

00:04:42.834 --> 00:04:45.300
She invented a game to keep
both her and her kids busy.

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:46.434
Check this out.

00:04:46.434 --> 00:04:49.934
[ Video game music ]

00:04:49.934 --> 00:04:52.267
[ Bell rings ]

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:54.901
[ Toy squeaking ]

00:04:54.901 --> 00:05:01.534
♪♪

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.300
Ah, I like that one
little, tiny mole.

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:05.133
There was like a bonus mole
that got in there.

00:05:05.133 --> 00:05:07.000
Cute. That was great.
Alright.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:08.400
Now, get out and let your --

00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:11.200
get your dad under there
and get me a real hammer.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:15.934
This last one is
@ashleycacioppo's dad

00:05:15.934 --> 00:05:17.200
got a little too immersed

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:19.601
in his virtual reality
plank experience.

00:05:19.601 --> 00:05:20.667
Watch this.

00:05:20.667 --> 00:05:22.767
-[ Laughing ]

00:05:22.767 --> 00:05:24.834
-Oh, oh, he did!

00:05:24.834 --> 00:05:27.868
[ Crash ]
-Oh, my!

00:05:27.868 --> 00:05:30.334
-[ Laughing ]
Oh! Oh!

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:31.334
Oh, my God.

00:05:31.334 --> 00:05:35.100
"Mom!
Mom, the TV broke Dad!"

00:05:35.100 --> 00:05:36.400
There you go, everybody.
That is

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.634
"What Are You Doing Wednesday."

